<h1>Fixture FAQ</h1>
<p>This page mirrors the shape of a real FAQ section: visible questions, each followed by a direct answer short enough to be lifted into a result. The AEO checks reward exactly that pattern, and the FAQPage schema in the head mirrors the same questions so the faq-schema check has nothing to deduct. Every answer stays inside the twenty to eighty word window the scanner accepts, and each heading below ends with a question mark.</p>
<h2>Why does the fixture exist?</h2>
<p>It exists so scanner assertions can pin exact scores against a copy that never changes. A live site drifts under you, so the suite serves these files from a temporary local server instead. Every deduction on every page is either designed into the markup or a scanner regression.</p>
<h2>How are the scores computed?</h2>
<p>Each check starts from one hundred points and subtracts a fixed weight per distinct failed check. The AI-readiness rubric deducts twenty-five for critical, ten for serious, five for moderate, and two for minor; the search rubric deducts twenty-five, twelve, six, and two. Grades follow the published thresholds.</p>
<h2>Which pages isolate which checks?</h2>
<p>The learning resource carries LearningResource JSON-LD, so the article-schema check credits it. The plain page omits article schema, a byline, statistics, and citations, so the GEO scanner reports exactly those four deductions. The thin page drops under the word threshold for the AI-readiness scanner.</p>
<h2>Can I edit the fixture?</h2>
<p>Yes, but treat the edit as a reviewed change. Update the fixture, re-run the offline suite, and adjust the pinned assertions only when the modification is deliberate. A change that makes a healthy page fail is a defect in either the fixture or the scanner.</p>
